iroh-relay 1.4.1: the server's ping interval, configurable (proposed upstream).

A relay pings a client after 15 s of its silence. iroh endpoints never see
it (they ping their relay every 15 s themselves); a silent client, such as
irpush's device on a phone, is woken by every one. RelayConfig::ping_interval
(and `ping_interval_secs` in the binary's config) lets an operator raise it,
default unchanged. `make desktop` builds irpush's own relay (`--serve`)
against this, pinging members after 130 min, as deploy/relay-ping.patch does
for the VPS's relay binary.

